From 10e7ca21858a459013b32104fa872aec0784e55b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:22:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Skip certified empty creator events during backfill

Why: unresolved created events survive indefinitely and links reconciliation
repeatedly fetches and Python-decodes their payloads. Most have a falsy creator,
so no future replica resolution can help until that event changes. A naive
anti-join changes SQLite traversal after ANALYZE and can change inheritance
ordering; JSON1 filtering also changes Python decode semantics.

Record disposable event-ID certificates only after successful falsy Python
decode. Invalidate on every event insert/update/delete, verify trigger coverage
in the read snapshot and writer transaction, and clear after coverage gaps.
Retire certificate data during recovery salvage and backup fill. Keep truthy
unresolved creators retryable and propagate transaction-loss errors.

Filter outside the original query using a nonflattened co-routine envelope.
Per-call EQP guards require original three/four-column traversal parity and
an exact outer PK-probe plan; unknown plans fall back to literal/Python filtering.

Do not change _differing_settled: its normal call chain already runs at the
30-second full-sweep floor. Earlier first/rebuild/schema/unknown invalidations
are required recovery paths. No repair, mirror, links, attachment or heal floor
is lengthened.

Proof: prior independent design and corrective implementation reviews;
RED-to-GREEN semantic, ordering, mutation, recovery and clobber regressions.
Parent canonical three-file run: 180 passed, including local clobber without
pull. All 12 importing consumer suites: 389 passed after test-only cleanup.
Full scripts/check: all 21 checks passed after test-only lint cleanup.
Independent 453-check audit of serial frozen three-arm 36-cell full-loop matrix:
all 12 counter triplets equal; 10 cold DB calls excluded per cell; all 72 pinned
live/shadow WAL endpoints >=400 MB. E1 mean paired 1k-to-20k warm backfill growth
reduction 79.872% checkpointed and 71.077% pinned, all six pairs positive.
This is synthetic warm-backfill evidence, not whole-loop CPU or a <=1% claim.
Production bytes match the measured frozen E1; later cleanup is test-only.
